    {
      "id": "W05-02",
      "status": "ACCEPTED",
      "executor_id": "qoder-desktop:/root/construction",
      "verifier_id": "qoder-desktop:/root/w0502_verifier_r1",
      "accepted_at": "2026-10-03T17:02:30.343362+00:00",
      "verdict": "ACCEPT_WITH_LIMITATIONS",
      "verdict_file": "receipts/W05/W05-02/independent_review_round1.json",
      "note": "card-level increment only; parent W05 and formal cases A04 and C11 are not accepted here. Reviewed at f214aa63, registered at HEAD 28262c96. 6 reservations and 5 limitations are carried on this row; blocking_issues is the empty array the verdict filed. Card step 3 is not met: workspace.write has no domain handler (obligation W05-02-domain-write-route), so the CLI writes nothing and the suite asserts that refusal.",
      "reservations": [
        "The delivered card behaviour 'one failing check drives a bounded repair' exists only at the unit-test layer, not as a routed CLI assertion: with the production writer refusing, CodingTask.Run returns before the check-result branch, so no W0502-* row can ever observe repair-after-failure. The suite's passing rows and TestFailingCheckDrivesBoundedRepair back this, and the Q3 expectation discloses it, but the routed face of deliverable 1 is 'refused write, real diff, real check', and the failing-check-driven-repair leg rides on the domain write route (obligation W05-02-domain-write-route).",
        "audit_receipt_w0502.py computes rather than echoes (its falsified-digest control fires, and it FAILs when the registry selector is removed), but it has two blind spots a later regeneration could exploit: (a) it never compares check_results.assertions to the length of the id list - a copied receipt claiming 999 assertions over 33 ids still passed all eight probes; (b) it audits receipt-against-working-tree only, never working-tree-against-committed-HEAD - a falsified coding_task.go with a consistently re-pinned artifact digest also passed. Neither applies to the current record (I verified tree==HEAD and digest==tree myself), so this is a hardening gap, not a present misstatement.",
        "lockedGit in coding_task_test.go verifies the pinned git path exists but not its sha256, while lockedGo in the routed suite does verify the digest; the git half of the toolchain discipline is one check weaker than the go half.",
        "The mutation matrix's killed/survived evidence is self-reported fields (run_status, run_rc, ids_lost); the auditor cross-checks counts but not that killed entries actually recorded FAIL. I independently re-ran two of the ten and both behaved as claimed (my own Q3-style CommandChecker mutation survived the routed suite with PASS/33 and died in TestCheckThatFailsIsCapturedAsAnExitCode; my own guard removal in Cancel was killed by exactly W0502-CANCEL-REFUSED-BEFORE-THE-QUEUE-WAS-CLEARED), so I trust the methodology, but the other eight rows stand on the executor's record.",
        "Minor prose drift in hashed artifacts: REVIEW_REQUEST_ROUND1.md says '20 hashed artifacts' (the receipt lists 21), CHECK_ID_ROUTING_MEASURED.md cites legacy.go:23-25 for the env reads (they now sit at 26-28 after servedChecks was added), and the auditor docstring enumerates nine probes while the run reports eight. None changes a measured value.",
        "Selector coupling is per-field: the registry lists task_id and check_id independently, so --task-id W12 --check-id W05-02 would route this suite (the program keys on RESEARCHOS_CHECK_ID alone, main.go:195). Assertion ids are card-namespaced and the suite emits only its own (row proven), so no cross-card borrowing is possible, but a mis-paired selector produces a green run under the wrong parent - inherited dispatcher design, disclosed nowhere in this card."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "I did not re-run the eight other mutants; two (Q3-survives, Q6-killed) were independently re-applied and matched, the rest were verified only for internal consistency of their recorded fields.",
        "I did not exercise LIVE mode, formal cases A04/C11, or the legacy ops/ci/runtime.py harness behind the forwarding path (the registry gate refused my bogus selector with NOT_IMPLEMENTED rc=3, which is the dispatcher-side half).",
        "I did not verify the earlier host-OOM disclosure (ops/remote_access/gateway) beyond noting this card's builds did not reproduce it on my runs.",
        "I did not audit the checkpoint registration machinery that will consume this verdict, nor parent W05's gate, nor the six rev-16 errata of the other cards beyond recomputing that each names the right receipt digest (4f065… family), right old pin and new pin 78ac9a1e…, and that a seventh W02-02 erratum honestly records its null pinned digest.",
        "I did not pursue whether a Goal-restarting-after-cancel row could land inside this write scope; I only confirmed the disclosure that it has no row is true against the 33 ids."
      ],
